# Release Notes

## Version 0.6.3
### ShaniOS
* The distro's install policy is config, not constants in the scripts:
  `install_policy` (os name, root/ESP labels, btrfs subvolumes and mount
  options, swapfile, image directory and image names, kernel cmdline files,
  UKI entry directory) is validated by the installer and exported to every
  step as `OSI_*`. Defaults are the ShaniOS layout, so a config that does
  not mention it behaves exactly as before.
* The installer decides who may install: `install_policy.admin_groups`
  (default `wheel`, `sudo`; root always, empty list disables). The reason is
  shown on the failed page instead of being printed into a terminal the user
  has to open.

## Version 0.6.2
### Fixes
* `available_translations` (set by the launcher before `init()`) survived the
  config load again, so the language list is the packaged one and not the
  fallback. A regression in 0.6.1, caught by installing the package into a
  shani-testbed slot and starting it there.

## Version 0.6.1
### ShaniOS
* New `dev/` harness: `sh dev/check.sh unit|a11y` builds the app the way the
  package installs it, in an Arch container with a headless X server and the
  AT-SPI bus, and walks the real GUI from Welcome to Restart Later. It
  screenshots every page and asserts the `OSI_*` environment the distro
  scripts receive.
* pytest suite for config loading, the `OSI_*` contract and the device model,
  also run in CI.

### Fixes
* The summary page rendered an empty box after Confirm: the state machine's
  page list is also what widgets ask "does this page exist?", and navigation
  had truncated it to the pages that can no longer be reached.
* Ctrl+T/W/Q, Ctrl+C in the terminal dialog and the test-mode Ctrl+S/F did
  nothing: GTK spells the modifier `<Control>`, not `<Ctl>`. Ctrl+R now
  reloads the page, as Hacking.md documents.
* The icon-only previous/next/reload/about buttons have accessible names.
* Config loading uses `safe_load` (a config file can no longer execute Python
  code) and no longer mutates the module defaults or multiplies
  `disk.min_size` on a second init.
* Device objects no longer share mount points or partitions between disks.
* The missing-script error is no longer overwritten by "Stopping
  installation".
* "No Disks avaliable" / "error that occured" typos; translation template
  regenerated for the new and changed strings.

## Version 0.6.0 — ShaniOS fork
First release of the ShaniOS fork of GNOME's os-installer. Forked at
upstream commit ba5b74d.

### ShaniOS
* Renamed to ShaniOS Installer (`org.shani.OsInstaller`), new icon, desktop
  entry, metainfo and GSettings schema; GResource prefix moved to
  `/org/shani/os-installer`. Binary and gettext domain are unchanged.
* Install scripts are run with `/bin/bash` instead of being exec'd directly.
* Optional root password on the encryption page (`OSI_ROOT_PASSWORD`).
* Summary page now lists disk encryption and root-password state.

### Fixes
* Generated usernames are used when `user.request_username` is off.
* Fixed-language provider no longer reads the config before it is loaded.
* `keyboard_language` fallback is a proper 2-tuple.
* Disk page stores the EFI partition device path, not its name.

## Version 0.5.1
* Adjust desktop selection
* Improve handling of missing images
* Log installation errors in terminal
* Fix app icon naming
* Updated translations

## Version 0.5.0
### Features
* Working translations independent of system languages
* Slideshow support, shown during installation
* Support for more scripting languages, e.g. Python and Lua
* Simpler disk/partition selection with expander rows
* Improved output terminal, copying support
* Faster search for timezone and region lists
* Config can be passed as CLI parameter
* Added translations (Farsi, Hebrew, Kabyle, Tamil, Vietnamese) and updated existing translations

### Config
* Add translation generator script
* Adjustable script paths
* Grouping of options for clearer structure
* Partiton acceptance option

### Internal
* Use bindings to custom objects in many places
* Split navigation out from main window
* Shared code for Continue, Confirm and Terminal button
* Make config variables lambda subscribable
* Restructure file structure for core functionality and widgets
* Run UI functions in GLib idle context
* Use fallback dict lookups (very useful)

## Version 0.4.0
* Use AdwNavigationView and other modern libadwaita widgets
* Added Desktop selection page
* Multiple-choice options for software/feature choices
* Password/pin can have confirmation fields and minimum length
* Optional username field added
* Fixes and internal refactorings for performance improvements
* Added translations (Arabic, Portuguese (Portugal), Romanian, Russian, Turkish, Urdu) and updated existing translations

## Version 0.3.0
* Lists scroll more intuitively and look nicer
* Optional welcome page with distro-customizable text added
* Summary page to confirm selection added
* Optional feature page added with which distributions can provide additional options
* Added and updated translations (Croatian, Dutch, Estonian, French, Georgian, German, Italian, Occitan, Polish, Portuguese (Brazil), Spanish, Swedish, Ukrainian)
* Keyboard page got overhauled to be simpler
* Many new config options for distributions, e.g. skipping the user and timezone page when using gnome-initial-setup

## Version 0.2.0
* GTK4 + libadwaita port
* lots of other overhauls

## Version 0.1.0
* Initial version